  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas remain within the broad, west-to-southwest wind field \nbetween Invest 90W to the southeast, and a low pressure area located\nfar to the north, near Iwo To. There is a col area between these two \nfeatures, located to the east of the coastal waters, which models\nsuggest will have more of an influence on Sunday as lighter, more \nsoutherly winds develop. This would better allow for island-effect \nshowers to develop in the afternoon, but this would largely depend on\nthe wind field around Invest 90W and its slow, subtle meandering. If\n90W, which remains very weak and disorganized, is fairly stationary \nfor the next day or so, the nearby col area would likely stay farther\neast of the Marianas, which would support a continuation of moderate\nwinds and fairly dry conditions tomorrow. For today, winds sustained\nat around 10 to 15 mph which kept most of the island convection off-\nshore. For Sunday night through early next week, isolated to low-end\nscattered showers are expected, associated with localized\nconvergence within the southwesterly, then becoming easterly to \nsoutheasterly, flow.\n\nThe main concern in the forecast for this next week is the\ndevelopment and movement of Invest 90W, currently situated east-\nnortheast of Weno, Chuuk near 8N156E. Latest model runs favor a \nslower development and movement than previous guidance indicated, \nand the associated increase in showers was delayed in the forecast \nuntil the latter half of the coming week. However, uncertainty \nremains high. The main concerns with Invest 90W are the flood \npotential from numerous to widespread locally heavy showers, as well \nas strong, gusty winds. Even if 90W struggles to organize and the \nwind field remains lackluster, a wet pattern is expected to develop,\nwith increasing certainty for the latter half of the coming week \nthrough next weekend. This far out, the precise certainty is low \nregarding when showers will become numerous as 90W approaches, and \nshowers were capped at 50 percent for Thursday night through \nSaturday, with wording included for locally heavy showers possible. \nAdditionally, exact wind speeds and timing remain highly uncertain, \nbut included wording for the likelihood of breezy conditions \ndeveloping at times later in the week, associated with 90W.",
